  "note": "Verified: with y = e^{w/H}, dy/y = dw/H and F_H(e^{w/H}) = H sin w/(πw), and y = t/2 ↔ w = −H log(2/t). Since h(2) = h(0) = 0, the integration by parts that follows has no boundary terms. hH_eq_conv is the literal statement up to the dummy rescaling v = w/H. hH_eq_u is the equivalent form that Lean actually integrates by parts."
